WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This film is, in many ways,
about Judaism,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
about things that survive
over generations,

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the different
relationships you can have

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.910
with your religion.
There is a joke that is so funny

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
about, basically, where th
100-year-old great-grandfather

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:19.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
finds out that Jonas Salk
cured polio,

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his first question is
"Was he Jewish?"

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:23.757 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Was he Jewish? Yeah.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
That taps into
a very Jewish thing,

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:30.797
which is Jews are very proud
of other Jewish accomplishments,

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.366
and he's so psyched when h
finds out Jonas Salk was Jewish.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.203
And nothing evidences this
probably, phenomena more tha

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
the book
"Great Jews in Sports"

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a book
every Jewish person has

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a small book,
but that is how much we want

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.114
to know what every Jewish
accomplishment in history

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.085
ever was, that we will tak
the six great Jews in sports

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make an entire book
about them.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:58.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] You mentioned --
Was it from the jump,

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
was it the idea that you would
play both characters?

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:05.265
Was there a time that -- I mean,
'cause it's not necessaril

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
a situation where that you had
to play both characters,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's such an accomplishmen
both technically

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.407
and as an actor, because you had
to take months off

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
between doing second halve
of the seasons, right?

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, no, we did the whole
first half as Herschel,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.881
and then we went back and di
the whole other half as Ben.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.717 size:81% position:41%
And it's not something
I went into lightly,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I actually tried
to get out of it several times

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
We actually did a table read
where Ike Barinholtz read

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Herschel role at one point
and he was hilarious.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.994 line:92%
And I remember thinking, like,

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We don't need me to do both
of them. We got Ike!"

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:43.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
But people, the other
filmmakers, really wanted me

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
to play both roles,
and, eventually,

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wrapped my head
around doing it.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, it was
incredibly complicated.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.579
But what I did find is I do no
like working with other actors

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I do prefer
working with myself.

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.417 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actors are tough,
and when you remove

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
as many of them
from the equation as possible,

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.289 line:92%
it makes things a lot easier

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Although, I think --
I would like to provide yo

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:08.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
the opportunity,
because you had a stand-in

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I imagine that was somebod
who, you know,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.467
there's not going to be a lo
of glory in being off-camera

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-But, obviously, this was

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
an incredibly important role
in this film.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.406 line:92%
-Yes, Ian Poake was his name

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:24.410
and he played opposite me
in almost every scene.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember telling him
specifically, like,

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:31.084
the better job you do, the les
it will seem like you exist.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:36.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like thriving for a complet
evaporation on your part,

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:39.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's the bull's-eye
you're trying to hit.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he really did
an amazing job,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was, like, in some ways
a very, like, selfless --

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, he was compensated
but, in some ways,

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:47.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very selfless thing
for him to do

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.604
was essentially act in an entire
movie with the understanding

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would be removed
from it later,

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.776 line:92%
and he played both roles.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whoever I wasn't playing,
he would play,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.681 line:92%
and he was very -- he was great.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was very,
like, malleable

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.617 line:92%
and would get my blocking.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:08.788
And sometimes, I would tell him,
like, "Just don't talk.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:12.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm hearing what you're saying
as I'm thinking of it,

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you just sit there
and look at me,"

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was like,
"Okay, no problem."

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.664 line:92%
And he was a great partner

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.798 line:92%
It was actually a lot of fun

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he made my performance
much better, yeah.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was really taken how quickl
you forget it is happening

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:32.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
at a separate time,
and I imagine so much work

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.647 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
went into that.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:37.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, ultimately, like,
you were saying,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you have to, like,
do all of this work to make it

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
then look invisible
for the audience, too.

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sort of remember --
not giving anything away -

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there's a moment later
in the film

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you start looking
more alike.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:52.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
You remember, "Oh.
This is Ben, not Herschel.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. No. It was another
one of those things

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
where, like, the better jo
we did, the less it would seem

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.705 size:81% position:41% line:92%
like we did something.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:00.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be like
if the funnier you were,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.276 line:92%
the less funny you seemed.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
The more our jobs
were done correctly,

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
the less we seemed like we wer
achieving anything special

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
or complicated in any way,
shape, or form,

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:17.156
which was a weird goal
to be chasing, but, yeah.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:21.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a worthy cause,
I thought, if nothing else

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:25.098
-You're also finding time
for another worthy cause.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:29.469
I have seen photos of some
of your ceramic work lately.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:30.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
These are ashtrays?

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:34.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I make ashtrays. I make vases
I make all sorts of things

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
This is an ashtray I made.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The part that I really want
to point out --

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is a lighter holder
on top, yes?

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.050
Well, no.
You can put your joint in there,

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.452 size:78% position:39%
and then you can put
your lighter in here.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ohh, look at that.
-Two little separate things.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:52.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a few different
designs around.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, do you keep those al
for yourself?

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:57.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do they stay in the family
Have you gifted them to anyone

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.965 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I've given some away.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll send you a vase,
if you want one.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That'd be very nice.
Thank you.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got one
coming coming your way.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, man, it's always
such a pleasure to see you

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.776 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Congrats on the film.

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really great.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I look forward
to the next time.

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:15.815
-Yeah, maybe one day, the worl
will go back to normal. Yeah

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I would like that.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would be nice.
Have a good one.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right,
Have a good one, sir.

